  "normative_review": [
    "Shared execution domain is the accepted default; session origin does not define enforcement scope.",
    "System and Agent retain baseline ownership; AgentRuntime is execution metadata, not another policy layer.",
    "Concurrent tasks and proposals remain allowed; domain policy application uses one trusted coordinator and expected active version.",
    "Full immutable snapshots do not claim atomic kernel hot switching or cross-domain transactions.",
    "Actual Broker/kernel readback remains distinct from stored intent; partial/unknown state is reported honestly.",
    "Connection/native adapter preserves original workspace/session/tool flows and capability-dependent feedback.",
    "Shared session projections read the same active domain facts; task cancellation does not remove shared rules.",
